module bindings.javascript.osTmpdirJoinedPathWithoutUniqueCreation;

// Node documents `os.tmpdir()` as "the operating system's default directory
// for temporary files" -- a directory every local account can write to and
// read -- and documents `fs.mkdtemp` as "creates a unique temporary
// directory" and `crypto.randomUUID` as a random identifier, which is why
// both are the recommended building blocks for anything placed there: the
// name underneath the shared directory must not be guessable, or another
// local user can pre-plant it, race its creation, or read what lands in it.
//
// So a function that joins further path segments onto `os.tmpdir()` and
// generates no unique name is building a predictable path for executable or
// readable content in a world-writable directory: a fixed segment, a hash of
// known strings, a process id or a timestamp all stay guessable, while
// `mkdtemp`/`mkdtempSync` and a `randomUUID` segment are the documented ways
// out. The two positive conjuncts and the negation all read the function's
// own `call:` tokens, which are exact per-callee entries: `in [...]` keeps
// `tmpdir` from matching a callee like `tmpdirish`, and namespace,
// aliased-namespace and bare-import spellings of the same call all appear
// among the listed forms.
//
// The path is reported at the function that builds it, not at the `mkdir` or
// `writeFile` that later creates it -- those regularly live in a different
// function, and the joined path is the whole defect: whoever receives it
// creates a directory the default umask leaves group- and world-readable.
// The fix this shape wants -- placing the cache under the application's own
// state directory with owner-only permissions -- removes the `tmpdir()` call
// and stops the report without touching anything else.
//
// Residual costs, stated rather than hidden. The conjuncts combine by
// co-occurrence, so a function that joins an unrelated path while separately
// consulting the temp directory reports as well. A unique name from any
// other generator still reports only when the generator is called outside
// this function -- a helper returning `randomUUID()` one call away leaves
// the joined form indistinguishable from a fixed one. And a `mkdtemp` or
// `randomUUID` call anywhere in the function neutralises the report even for
// an unrelated fixed-name join in the same body, the false-negative
// direction. A base built by string concatenation or a template literal
// rather than a path `join` is not read at all.
binding osTmpdirJoinedPathWithoutUniqueCreation {
  query pattern presenceNode where node.scope == "function"
    and node.context.language == "javascript"
    and node.context.call in ["tmpdir", "os.tmpdir", "node:os.tmpdir"]
    and node.context.call in ["join", "path.join", "node:path.join", "posix.join"]
    and not containsAny(node.context.call, ["mkdtemp", "randomUUID"])
  emit issue code.InsecureTempFile at node
}
